ur existing SAP Build Process Automation projects.  See SAP Note 3394899  and Environments, Create an Environment, and Share an Environment. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-25\nValid as Of: 2024-01-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3616 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhanced Email Notification Domain\nDescription: Notification emails now use the SAP Build Work Zone runtime domain, making it possible to launch hyperlinks in the notification emails to open directly in the native SAP Build Work Zone Advanced mobile app.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-01-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3617 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Wizard Layout in Workspaces\nDescription: Workspace administrators can create wizard-like predefined processes, to help users complete complex business flows. The wizards can include multiple stages and steps, and cards and widgets can be added to them.   Card developers can interact with the wizard to leverage wizard events and context updates. For more information and sample cards, see Wizard Developer Guide (Github).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-01-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3618 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Workspace: Access Levels for Non-Members\nDescription: Workspace administrators can define specific users lists and users who can access the workspace as non-members.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-01-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3619 --